    "knowledge_point": "Integrating Using Arcsecant",
    "problem": "$\\int \\frac{11}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
    "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{arcsec}\\,x.\n$$\n\nThen we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{11}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =11\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =11arcsecx+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
